Subject: [PATCH] drm: rotate fullscreen direct scanout buffers on SM8550

Allow normal, uncropped fullscreen buffers to be scanned out on outputs
transformed by 90 or 270 degrees. Carry a separate sampling transform with
the output buffer and program primary-plane rotation with atomic KMS.

Keep the existing GPU composition fallback when TEST_ONLY rejects the
buffer, including unsupported modifiers, formats and DPU source sizes.
Reject this path on legacy, libliftoff and multi-GPU backends. Reset the
rotation when replacing the scanout buffer with a composed frame.

This changes wlr_output_state: rebuild Sway and other wlroots consumers.
Based on wlroots 0.19.3; requires the SM8550 DPU inline rotation patch.

